From: echo-penguin
Subject: [PATCH] fonts: prefer SUN12x22 as the console font

CONFIG_FONT_8x16 is selected by the MediaTek video Kconfig, and 8x16 outranks SUN12x22 off SPARC,
so fbcon would pick 8x16 (120x30 characters, hard to read on the 5.5" panel). fbcon=font: would
lengthen the bootloader command line, which hangs warm reboots; give SUN12x22 the preference it
has on SPARC instead.
---
diff --git a/lib/fonts/font_sun12x22.c b/lib/fonts/font_sun12x22.c
index 057b0bf368a..0fbe1ecc663 100644
--- a/lib/fonts/font_sun12x22.c
+++ b/lib/fonts/font_sun12x22.c
@@ -6159,6 +6159,7 @@ const struct font_desc font_sun_12x22 = {
 #ifdef __sparc__
 	.pref	= 5,
 #else
-	.pref	= -1,
+	/* echo-penguin: the console font on cronos (80x21 on 960x480), chosen without fbcon=font: */
+	.pref	= 5,
 #endif
 };
